# =============================================================================
# PopolaLoom .gitignore
#
# Intentionally NEVER ignored (DevolaFlow tracked surfaces, see bottom note):
#   .local/**, .rules/**, AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/**
# =============================================================================


# === OS / IDE ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/


# === Cursor IDE (per-user state) ===
# Ignore everything under .cursor/ (logs, scratch, per-user agent state, etc.),
# BUT keep the compiled DevolaFlow rules under .cursor/rules/ tracked. The
# leading-slash-free pattern matches the .cursor folder at any depth, and the
# negation re-includes the rules subdir so the compile step (devola-init local)
# can publish .cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc into version control.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/


# === Python ===
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/


# === Node / JS ===
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.yarn/


# === Env / Secrets ===
# Ignore .env files (which typically hold API keys / DB URLs / secrets) but
# always keep .env.example checked in as the canonical schema reference.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# === Logs / Temp / Scratch ===
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
temp/
*.bak


# === PopolaLoom runtime artifacts ===
# popolad daemon 的运行时产物 (出处: spec.md §10 路径表):
#   ~/.popola/                       — 用户级 daemon 目录 (sock / pid / events / blobs)
#   popola.sock                      — repo 内调试 socket
#   events/                          — NDJSON event log 目录 (CloudEvents 1.0)
#   state.sqlite                     — LangGraph SqliteSaver 持久化文件
~/.popola/
popola.sock
events/
state.sqlite

# === PopolaLoom auxiliary build artifacts ===
arktower.db
.benchmarks/
.coverage
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# v0.6.1 (CI hotfix): the auto-merge gate config at
# .workflow/automerge.yaml is consumed by both the GitHub workflow
# (`.github/workflows/automerge.yml`) AND the unit-test
# `tests/test_automerge_gate.py::test_repo_workflow_automerge_yaml_loads_cleanly`,
# so it MUST be tracked. The surrounding `.workflow/*` block stays
# ignored so per-checkout scratch artefacts (e.g. evidence JSON the
# workflow drops alongside) do not pollute git. NOTE: we use
# `.workflow/*` (glob children) instead of `.workflow/` (the dir
# itself) because git refuses to re-include a path whose parent dir
# is excluded — see `man gitignore`.
.workflow/*
!.workflow/automerge.yaml
.cursor/


# === PopolaLoom local agent workspace (v0.7.0+) ===
# v0.7.0 policy change (per user feedback v0.6.1 item #1): the `.local/`
# tree — local agent workspace covering handoffs, memory, feedbacks, tasks,
# specs, eval_reports, and `.agent/` state — is now a *local-only* working
# surface and is no longer committed to git. Older v0.6.x checkpoints did
# track these files; from v0.7.0 onward the directory is gitignored. The
# on-disk files are preserved by intent — only their git-tracked status
# changes (a one-time `git rm --cached -r .local/` un-tracks them).
.local/

# =============================================================================
# DO NOT IGNORE — DevolaFlow tracked surfaces
# =============================================================================
# v0.7.0 policy change (per user feedback v0.6.1 item #1): `.local/` was
# previously listed here as a tracked surface, but is now gitignored (see
# explicit `.local/` ignore rule above). The DevolaFlow toolchain
# (devola-init local + the .rules/ governance compiler) still produces the
# surfaces below, which MUST remain tracked in git so the workflow is
# reproducible across clones / CI:
#
#   .rules/                              — governance source layers
#   .rules/compile-config.yaml           — compiler config (template seed)
#   .rules/.compile-hashes.json          — drift-detection hashes (auto-gen)
#   AGENTS.md                            — compiled corpus for Codex / generic
#   .cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc    — compiled corpus for Cursor IDE
#
# None of the rules above match these paths. If a future rule starts shadowing
# them, add an explicit `!path/here` negation in the appropriate section.
# =============================================================================
